Expose Jellyfin's Genres array on MediaItem.

aiojellyfin's TypedDict-driven mashumaro decoder silently drops any
JSON key that isn't declared on the TypedDict, so even when a caller
passes `ItemFields.Genres` and Jellyfin returns `"Genres": [...]`, the
field is stripped before the caller sees it. Declare `Genres` on
`MediaItem` so it survives decoding.

diff --git a/aiojellyfin/models.py b/aiojellyfin/models.py
index 853bb82..352e201 100644
--- a/aiojellyfin/models.py
+++ b/aiojellyfin/models.py
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@ class MediaItem(TypedDict, total=False):
     AlbumArtists: list[ArtistItem]
     MediaSources: list[MediaSource]
     NormalizationGain: int | None
+    Genres: list[str]
 
 
 MediaItemT = TypeVar("MediaItemT", bound=MediaItem)
